{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_vrtx_01Qfbdq4wXBfrUXK919kVdcv","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-4-7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great, so `loops_dir` and `skills_dir` are both being set in `buildLearningPrompt`. The variables get resolved in the template, and the template uses them in text like:\n```\n直接写入：`{{skills_dir}}/candidate_skill_{n}.md`\n```\n\nAfter resolution, this becomes:\n```\n直接写入：`/Users/sunquan/ai_coding/CODING/rick/.rick/skills/candidate_skill_{n}.md`\n```\n\nThe string \"skills_dir\" is gone. Same for \"loops_dir\".\n\nThe test checks for `\"loops_dir\" not in output` and `\"skills_dir\" not in output`. \n\nSo the real issue is that the test is looking for the literal string \"loops_dir\" in the output, but since the template resolves these variables, they get replaced with their actual paths. The simplest fix would be to add a variables section to the dry-run output that explicitly shows the resolved values, or update the test to check for the actual path strings instead. I need to trace through how `buildLearningPrompt` derives those directory values so I can extract them for the debug output.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e433f41c-cd46-4988-b35b-60af1cb85d96","uuid":"ce8556b9-7ec8-45ee-8181-324b71b19af2"}
